From 66672de3b21e2a8aaaee64f3457d779ed01e5cc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:00:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] texture: product cut out of its photo, front-only
 mapping, sides from the product; CAD front check

- server/photo_cut.py: the product cut out of its photo, cached as image.cut.png (+ .cut.json with
  the box, method, keystone quad, colours). Plain studio background: border flood (~0.1 s). Cluttered
  (the LG fridge between its neighbours): U^2-Netp salient object via onnxruntime on CPU (4.6 MB
  model fetched once into <DATA_DIR>/cache/models, ~0.1-0.3 s), the largest central object whose
  aspect matches the part's W x H; a catalogue crop the product fills stays whole. A slight keystone
  of a box face is straightened (only when the model's front is a rectangle). Dominant body / trim
  colours sampled by k-means with the outline band weighted; finish cue from the listing words.
- meshgen.project (ASSET_PHOTO_CUT, default on): the cut-out fitted to the front footprint of the
  front-facing visible triangles (normal within 60 deg, was 70) instead of the whole bbox; far
  background fades to the body colour. Old path kept as _project_legacy.
- meshgen.recolor (ASSET_SIDE_COLOR, default on): the sampled body colour on Hunyuan meshes and boxes,
  CAD pieces left the default grey (small ones take the trim), template shell roles still in the
  template default; a subtle PBR cue (metal 0.35/0.35, plastic 0/0.7, painted 0/0.5; photo 0.12/0.5
  for metal). decal_box sides in the body colour.
- CAD orientation (ASSET_SCAD_ORIENT): meshgen.orientation compares what the front (+Z) and the back
  show (pieces, detail share, relief, photo correlation); a backwards model is turned 180 deg about Y
  (turn_around) before the photo goes on. SCAD_PROMPT now spells out the front (handles, controls,
  seams at Z=D, proud); an appliance whose CAD front is a flat slab gets one relief feedback pass.
- assets.retexture + `python -m server.warm --retexture`: every variant re-textured from its own
  geometry (scad.glb, the cached raw Hunyuan mesh, the cached template plan, the box), OFFLINE: $0.
- Asset.texture records how each model was textured.
- onnxruntime added to the dependencies (uv.lock: onnxruntime, flatbuffers, protobuf).

